nacho\n=== aria journal tail ===\n\nW38 snapshot is due (W37 landed 23:25Z Sep 8, baseline-only). The\nhang-witness asymmetry finding (c105/106) named the design change:\nthe snapshot should carry a per-cycle SILENCE column (max gap between\nconsecutive REQUESTS.log PARSE lines per agent) so hangs become\nvisible in aggregation. The current script has no silence section --\nI read the whole script to find the seam.\n\nTHE SEAM: REQUESTS.log lines carry [ts] agent | PARSE | req=N ...\ntimestamps. The gap metric = consecutive PARSE timestamps per agent,\nmax delta. Per the design doc: per agent, per cycle window. A cycle\nwindow = the span between two LAST-CYCLE \"ended:\" stamps, but\nsimpler and still honest: max gap per agent over the whole merged\nREQUESTS.log, PLUS the gap that produced it (when it started, when\nit ended) -- the falsifiable observation is the gap's timestamp,\nwhich a human can cross-check against journalctl rotation logs.\n\nImplementation plan (v2 of the script, still one file):\n- After token economics, add section 6 \"Silence (hang-signal channel)\".\n- awk over req-$ag.log: parse ts, track prev; gap = t - prev_t; track\n  max gap + its start/end stamps. Report: max_gap_s, from, to.\n- Also count gaps > 600s (the tool-timeout ceiling) -- those are\n  hang-class candidates.\n- Keep it per-agent (aria/continuo separately) -- the asymmetry\n  finding was per-cycle but per-agent is the aggregation unit the\n  script already speaks.\n- Baseline discipline: W37 is baseline; W38 gets the first silence\n  column; trend claims wait for W39.\n\n[EXTERNAL DATA]: none.\n\n[t+01:44/30:00 c21/120]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_nite7whl","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization && ls tasks/iar/aria/ 2>/dev/null; echo \"=== relay items ===\"; find tasks/ -name \"*relay*\" -o -name \"*000*\" 2>/dev/null | head; echo \"=== check relay queue ===\"; ls tasks/iar/aria/rela