es model requests; audit.log logs at completion, so a hung tool is invisible) and the 1800s budget burned. The tool layer HAD a timeout param but defaulted to 3600s -- longer than the whole cycle budget -- and no caller ever passed one. Fix: iar-exec-default-timeout defcustom, 600s default, in execute_code_local.el (commit ae37766, pushed to sophon-bare). One hung call now costs max 1/3 cycle and the sentinel fires with partial output + TIMEOUT marker. Open question for you (no action needed tonight): the hang itself is still undiagnosed -- rg completed in 6ms when re-run, no FIFO/huge-file trigger found; suspect harness-side dispatch stall, possibly gptel-fork related. If it recurs WITH the timeout, the [TIMEOUT] marker will tell us where it died. Also: c64's grace template says 'TIME LIMIT REACHED' whatever fired it (cap vs timeout) -- minor, but it misleads forensics.</p>\n1788861356 aria-cycle: <p>flag (aria c66): instrument upgrade request, interactive-session item. The c66 stall census proved the grace requests' histories carry +5..+9 anomalous messages (duplicated tool results, assistant-msg runs) -- but the REQUESTS.log START tail cap (2 msgs, iar--reqlog-payload-tail in iar-request-log.el) cannot show WHAT they are. Discriminator: raise the tail cap to 6 msgs to match the roles field (3-line change, same file). No urgency -- the census pattern re-fires on the next stall either way; with the 6-msg tail the next stall would hand us the full mechanism instead of another hypothesis list.</p>\n1788864936 aria-cycle: <p>[aria c68] DRAIN msg 577: the tail-cap flag is RESOLVED -- interactive session landed iar-request-log-tail-msgs=6 (<a href=\"http://i.ar\">i.ar</a> 01533ea, suite 1125/1125). Also found this cycle: the sophon <a href=\"http://i.ar\">i.ar</a> checkout was at 706f4e4 (continuo c133) when c67 started, so c67 ran WITHOUT the budget trailer/600s timeout/6-msg tail -- the ExecStartPre heal fixes ownership, not staleness. Checkout now pulled to 01533ea; 