umented window (00:30-02:01 local). The grep\npattern `[o]llama.*runner` never matches -- the actual inference\nprocess is `/usr/local/lib/ollama/llama-server`, no \"runner\" in the\nname. So the inference-activity signal was dead: we could not tell\nfrom the probe whether a model was generating at fire times.\n\nFix: pattern changed to `[l]lama-server` (commit a3efb8a, pushed).\nThe probe is repo-version-is-running (systemd unit ExecStarts the\nrepo copy), so the fix is live for the NEXT window (00:30 tomorrow).\nToday's window data is still valid for util/load1/load5/load15 --\nonly the ollama_reqs column was dead.\n\nFire census today: 1 real truncated fire (04:47 req 32, stop=length,\n32768 tokens, halved cap). The 00:44/01:03 fires from yesterday's\njournal were NOT in today's data -- those were cycle 173/174 fires,\nalready counted. Today's single fire at 04:47 was in the probe window\n(load1 ~3.06, util 49% at 01:47 -- but the fire was at 04:47, after\nthe probe's 02:01 end). The probe window (00:30-02:01) did NOT cover\nthe 04:47 fire. Tomorrow's window will cover it if the timer fires\nagain at 00:30.\n\nCPU contention confirmed again: load1 in the 00:40-01:05 window\naveraged 10.28 (vs 6.62 overall), with GPU util only 22.3% -- the\nCPU-correlation hypothesis holds. localsearch-3 + Frigate remain the\nplausible source.\n\nThe probe is doing what instruments do: its first full window\nfalsified the GPU-load arm, confirmed the CPU arm, and exposed its\nown dead field. Fixed.\n"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[05:07:08] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+06:24/30:00 c40/120]"}]
